    <h2>PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE</h2>

    <div class="experience-item">
        <div class="job-title">Senior QA Engineer/ Technical QA</div>
        <div class="company">Partner Associates International Co., Ltd. — IT Solutions</div>
        <div class="date-location">May 2023 — July 2026 | Yangon, Myanmar</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Serve as the sole Technical QA Engineer within a 10-person QA team (1 Manager, 2 Senior Domain QA, 7 Junior/Interns), owning all technical QA initiatives including automation, infrastructure validation, deployment support, security testing, and code review.</li>
            <li>Lead end-to-end QA validation for enterprise-scale government and identity management systems across Web, Mobile, Desktop, API, and hardware-integrated platforms (passport readers, signature devices, biometric peripherals).</li>
            <li>Own deployment validation, smoke testing, and UAT support for QA and Pre-Production environments; manage PR approvals, environment readiness assessments, and release gate verification.</li>
            <li>Design, configure, and validate Azure DevOps CI/CD pipelines for build verification, automated test execution, clean deployment steps, and release quality checks.</li>
            <li>Develop and maintain automation frameworks using Python, JavaScript, Playwright, Postman Collections, and Locust for regression testing, API validation, and concurrent load testing with multiple users.</li>
            <li>Conduct comprehensive security testing including authentication, authorization, API gateway routing, public token validation, and access control verification.</li>
            <li>Validate server performance, security posture, and infrastructure stability across Windows Server and Ubuntu Linux environments.</li>
            <li>Collaborate directly with Development, Infrastructure, PMO, BA teams, and client stakeholders in DRB sessions, requirement reviews, and issue confirmation meetings.</li>
            <li>Prepare UAT sign-off reports, test coverage analysis, and release readiness documentation; calculate test completion metrics and drive releases meeting >95% pass thresholds with zero critical ground impact.</li>
            <li>Mentor junior QA engineers and interns through testcase reviews, technical knowledge sharing, issue analysis, and QA best practices; approve all test deliverables before release cycles.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="achievements">
            <strong>Key Achievements:</strong>
            <ul>
                <li>Successfully delivered 7 enterprise government digital transformation projects to production with zero critical defects, improved system performance, and enhanced operational stability.</li>
                <li>Created comprehensive deployment validation guides and environment issue documentation, reducing deployment failures and streamlining release cycles for UAT and production.</li>
                <li>Optimized Azure DevOps pipelines by eliminating redundant steps, implementing build prerequisite checks, and standardizing clean deployment workflows.</li>
                <li>Established reusable API automation collections and structured QA validation frameworks, significantly improving regression efficiency and test coverage.</li>
                <li>Maintained enterprise release quality thresholds consistently exceeding organizational UAT acceptance standards.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

